      "writtenOn": "2026-04-23T00:06:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "**Hex Parsing Truncation Risk:** In `CommandLineManager::parseHex`, `strtol` returns a `long`. You are directly assigning this to a `uint16_t`. If a user inputs a PID/VID larger than `0xFFFF`, it will silently truncate and attempt to connect to the wrong device.\n\n**Remediation:** Check if the parsed `long` exceeds `std::numeric_limits\u003cuint16_t\u003e::max()` before casting, and return `std::nullopt` if it overflows.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 78,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 94,
        "endChar": 2
      },
      "revId": "eee15e6508ade570d3670bc2f00d613d0a77d9c7",
